{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-emergence-to-quantum-flat","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:emergence-to-quantum-flat","kind":"proposition","title":"From Tannakian emergence to 2-group quantum flatness","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-self-dual-2group","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-flatness"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-emergence-to-quantum-flat"],"tags":["tannaka-krein","2-group","instanton"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.emergence_to_quantum_flat","text":"emergence-to-quantum-flat.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/emergence-to-quantum-flat.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:emergence-to-quantum-flat\"></a><p>For a QOU meeting the categorical volume constraint, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q \\cong \\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code>. The inner-automorphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{INN}(G_q)</code> governs the quantum flatness condition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A = B</code>, reproducing the instanton equation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_A^- = 0</code> under simplicity. Quantum flatness operates as a derived consequence of the instanton axiom.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/emergence-to-quantum-flat.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.25.7"}
